[E-REFL] Error: `rfl` can't prove this
    ╭─[ reject/match-refines-goal-once.sw:23:37 ]
    │
 16 │ ╭─▶     match step n with
    ┆ ┆   
 18 │ ├─▶       | None => None
    │ │                          
    │ ╰────────────────────────── this `match`
    │ 
 23 │         | None => Witness (Cons k rest) rfl
    │                                         ─┬─  
    │                                          ╰─── `(match …) rest (step n)` and `None` aren't equal
    │     
    │     Note 1: `rfl` proves `a = b` only when both sides compute to the same value
    │     
    │     Note 2: `(match …)` is a `match` written inside `run`, marked "this `match`" above; the compiler turned it into a function that source can't name. The same `match` written again is another such function, equal to it only if neither calls the definition it's written in. To state a lemma about it, make it a local `def` in its arm and refer to it as `owner.name`, where `owner` is the definition it is written in (docs/syntax.md, "Proving things about a definition with an inner `match`")
